M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#       compiled in if the option specified is not enabled.[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#       specified is enabled. Source files added with optofffile are[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#       Source files added with optfile are compiled in if the option[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#       kernel config.[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#       then turned on by including "options optname" in a[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#       "defoption" declares the name of a kernel option. These are[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#    optofffile optname sourcefile.c[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#    optfile optname sourcefile.c[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#    defoption optname[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# The syntax for defining optional source files is:[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#       Such a file is always included automatically in every kernel.[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#    file sourcefile.c[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# The syntax for adding a regular source file is:[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# [39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# kernel source, that is, src/kern.[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# Note: All source file names are relative to the top directory of the[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# Kernel definition file syntax:[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m############################################################[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#       information about what this means, see below.[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#       a device foo that is attached to a device bar. For more [39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#       supposed to be "attached" to anything. The second line enables[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#       a wildcard. The first line enables a device foo that is not[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#       where the % is either a number or a star, which is treated as[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#    device foo% at bar%[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#    device foo%[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# The syntax for turning on a device driver is:[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#       specially, and is just "debug" without the "options".[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#       The act of compiling with debug info is (has to be) handled[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#       for more information.[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#       A previous "defoption" must have been seen first. See below[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#    options optname[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# The syntax for turning on a kernel compile option is:[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#       You can also include other files using the same syntax.[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#       else useful.[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#       because the system must be defined before you can do much[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#       This should come second, after the architecture. This is[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#    include conf.kern[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# The syntax for including the system definition is:[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#       This must come before anything else in the kernel config.[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#    arch archname[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# The syntax for specifying the processor architecture to use is:[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# Kernel config file syntax:[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m############################################################[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# The documentation for the syntax of these files follows.[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# will likely make a mess and produce mysterious error messages.[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# probably get the host system's kernel config utility, which[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# "./config", not just "config" - in the latter case you will[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# right directory (the same one this file is in) and run it as[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# Note: when running the config script, be sure to be in the[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;12r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# others like it) and rerun the config script.[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# To add new files to the system, you need to edit this file (or[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# facilities for a particular kernel build.[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# a kernel config (such as ASST1) is used to select options and [39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# are declared by conf.kern and the various files it includes. Then[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# The idea is that the files, options, and facilities in the system[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m# Machine-independent kernel config definitions.[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h7[2;11r8M[1;14r[2;1H[36m#[39m(B[m[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[13d[J[14d[?12l[?25h[14;1H[?1049l[23;0;0t[?1l>[?2004l[?2004h]0;john@debian: ~/cs161/src/kern/conf[01;32mjohn@debian[00m:[01;34m~/cs161/src/kern/conf[00m$ vi conf.kern
